# Code owners for StellarCred
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a pull request
# touches.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS: when several patterns match the same file, the LAST
# matching rule wins. This file is therefore written general-to-specific —
# broad catch-alls first, narrow overrides after. Moving a block without
# re-checking what follows it will silently change who reviews what.
#
# Why this file exists: StellarCred is a ZK credential layer whose trust
# anchor is the pair (on-chain contract, ZK circuit). A docs typo and a
# change to proof verification do not deserve the same amount of review.
#
# Owners below are the repository maintainers. When the project forms review
# teams, replace these handles with team slugs (for example
# `@ToluLabs/protocol` for contracts/circuits) — a team slug that does not
# exist or lacks write access is silently ignored by GitHub, so verify any
# new slug has write access before relying on it.
#
# Review expectations per area are documented in CONTRIBUTING.md
# ("Review routing") and the full checklist in docs/THREAT_MODEL.md.

# ── Baseline: everything ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Starting point. Every path below refines this, so nothing falls through
# to an unreviewed state.
/*                             @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── Frontend, general ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UI, components, and pages. Refined further below for the issuance path
# and the SDK.
/frontend/                     @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── Trust anchor: contracts and circuits ────────────────────────────────────
# Highest scrutiny. Contracts decide which issuers are trusted and whether
# a proof is accepted; circuits decide what a proof can even assert. A
# change here can be technically correct, well tested, and still break the
# guarantees the whole system rests on. Review against
# docs/THREAT_MODEL.md, and expect the reasoning to be checked, not just
# the diff.
/contracts/                     @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/circuits/                      @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock pin soroban-sdk and the git-sourced UltraHonk
# verifier at exact revisions for cryptographic compatibility. A bump here
# can silently change verifier behaviour or invalidate existing proofs, so
# it is reviewed alongside the contracts it affects.
/Cargo.toml                     @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/Cargo.lock                     @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Committed verification keys, proofs, and public inputs are the artifacts
# the contract tests verify against. Regenerating them by hand rather than
# through the documented circuit build would let a broken circuit look green.
/fixtures/                      @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Circuit toolchain and test-vector generation. Nargo.toml pins the Noir
# version; the scripts build circuits and regenerate fixtures, so a change
# here can alter proof output without changing any circuit source.
/circuits/Nargo.toml            @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/circuits/scripts/              @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── Issuance and signing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# frontend/app/api/ is the issuance path. ISSUER_PRIVATE_KEY is read here,
# and a credential is only as trustworthy as the signing step. A
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix slipping in, or a change to the `prehash: false`
# signing option, would let anyone mint credentials.
/frontend/app/api/              @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# The signing helper and the KYC webhook sit outside app/api/ but are the
# same trust path: the webhook accepts third-party identity assertions and
# the signer produces the signature the circuit later verifies.
/frontend/lib/issuer-signer.ts  @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/frontend/lib/persona-webhook.ts @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/frontend/lib/error-reporting.ts @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Next middleware runs ahead of every request and is a common place for
# auth and header handling to drift.
/frontend/middleware.ts         @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Contract bindings are generated, but they are the client-facing view of
# the trust anchor and are hand-edited often enough to be worth routing.
/frontend/packages/issuer-registry/   @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/frontend/packages/proof-registry/    @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── SDK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The published integrators' surface. Breaking a signature here breaks
# downstream projects on an npm package that cannot be unpublished.
/frontend/packages/sdk/         @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── Indexer service ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Independent of the on-chain verification path, so normal review depth
# applies, but it reads chain state and republishes it to consumers.
/services/indexer/              @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── CI/CD, release, and supply chain ────────────────────────────────────────
# Workflows run with repository credentials and the release workflow
# publishes to npm. Treat a workflow diff like a signing-path diff.
/.github/workflows/             @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/.github/dependabot.yml         @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# Makefile and deny.toml are build and supply-chain policy: they decide
# which commands run and which crates and licences are allowed.
/Makefile                       @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/deny.toml                      @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01

# ── Policy, ADRs, and security documentation ───────────────────────────────
# The ADRs record why the load-bearing trust-model choices were made, and
# CONTRIBUTING requires citing them for changes in those areas. These
# documents set the review bar the rest of this file relies on.
/CHANGELOG.md                   @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/SECURITY.md                    @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/SUPPORT_POLICY.md              @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/VERSION_COMPATIBILITY.md       @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/docs/                          @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @nonchalanttee22-lgtm @Psalmuel01
